        "**Data Types**\n",
        "In R and in programing, data types are the classifications we give different kinds of information pieces. R data types:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Numeric: Any number with or without a decimal point, 23, 0.03 and a number null value NA\n",
        "2. Character: Any groupding of characters on your keyboard (letters, numbers, spaces, symbols, etc) or text. Most strings are surrounded by sing quotes '...' or double quotes \"...\" sometimes you will hear this type referred to as \"string\"\n",
        "3. Logical: This data type only has two possible values-either TRUE or FALSE (without quotes). It is helpful to think of logical types or booleans as on and off, yes or no question.\n",
        "4. Vectors: A list of related data that is all the same type\n",
        "5. NA: This data type represents the absence of a value, an is represented by the keyword NA (without quotes) but it has its own significance in the content of different types. There is numeric NA, a character NA, a logical NA."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "WeHzaOnX1yBH"
      }
    },
